  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 is the dominant factor (0.706–0.725 vs ~0.52–0.54 for scgpt), and within scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l, transformer aggregation + weighted fusion (config_007, 0.725) is the best. However, we have not yet tested whether the image encoder choice matters when paired with the strong scvi_n200 encoder—resnet50 was only tested with the weaker scgpt. This experiment (scvi_n200 + resnet50 + transformer + weighted) directly tests whether resnet50 can match or approach imagenet_vit_l in the best-performing regime. If it performs comparably, it may offer a cheaper path; if it lags, we confirm imagenet_vit_l is essential and can focus remaining budget on fine-tuning around config_007. This is the highest-information single experiment: it resolves the image-encoder question under the proven best RNA/aggregation/fusion settings. Expected cost: ~3.5–4.5 GPU hours (resnet50 is smaller than ViT-L, so likely at or slightly below config_007's 3.60 h, though transformer aggregation adds overhead)."
}

